From 9132178aa347353b8b45cdcb887ede5c4cb66ea0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:49:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: the renderer enters and leaves native output with
 what it can draw

The renderer decided native output once, from the picture it was
configured with, and only left it when native output was disabled for
the session. That gave two wrong outcomes:
- A renderer configured for the ordinary output never entered native
  output: the first picture came without its RPU (an unreadable RPU,
  a cut file), or the output switched to a transport mode after the
  renderer was configured (a refresh-rate switch after the first
  picture, a GUI resolution change). The whole playback stayed on the
  ordinary output.
- Conditions that only make native output impossible for the moment
  went through the frame-failure counter, which after two seconds
  disabled native output until Kodi restarted: a mode that cannot carry
  the transport (leaving fullscreen with "adjust refresh rate: always"
  and a 1080p GUI), zoom or stretch, a picture pillarboxed at an odd
  column (x = 127 for a 3586-pixel wide picture), and pictures in system
  memory (the base renderer claimed native output but cannot draw it).

Native output now follows what the pictures ask for and what the
renderer can draw now, checked for every picture in ConfigChanged():
- It starts with a picture that asks for it and that the renderer can
  draw: a VAAPI surface in NV12/P010/P012/P016, no rotation, and a
  geometry that shows the whole picture at its own aspect ratio inside
  the 3840x2160 raster.
- It ends, without disabling it for the session, when the verdict
  (mode, display, disabled) or the geometry no longer allows it, and
  starts again when they do. A picture without metadata still does not
  end it (it is only not drawn).
- Both change only with the mode, the view settings or a failure (which
  disables native output for the session), so the renderer cannot
  alternate from picture to picture. The geometry is computed on the
  render thread after each ManageRenderArea() and published atomically
  to the player thread, which never reads a rectangle being updated.
- The horizontal position and width of the picture are moved inwards to
  even columns (at most one pixel each side), as the 4:2:2 transport
  needs, instead of refusing every frame; full-screen and letterboxed
  geometry is unchanged.
- The 8-bit transport format is chosen only when the renderer draws the
  picture natively; otherwise the output keeps its ordinary depth.
